</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Main Results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multiple-Choice Tasks.</span> Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that our approach consistently outperforms baseline PEFT methods. For Qwen2.5-1.5B, SVD with LoRA improves scores from 46.99% to 49.77%. For Qwen2.5-7B, SVD with Prompt Tuning increases scores from 45.49% to 50.29%. For LLaMA3.1-8B, SVD with LoRA boosts scores from 42.89% to 47.80%. Despite occasional MC1 score drops, MC2 and MC3 improvements ensure overall better performance, highlighting SVD’s effectiveness in enhancing truthful answer selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Open-Ended Generation Tasks.</span> Table <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows that our approach improves performance across all datasets. For Qwen2.5-1.5B, SVD with LoRA increases the score from 44.71% to 45.73%. For Qwen2.5-7B, SVD with P-Tuning v2 raises the score from 62.80% to 64.43%. For LLaMA3.1-8B, SVD with LoRA boosts the score from 45.78% to 46.54%. This demonstrates SVD’s effectiveness in enhancing model responses.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commonsense Reasoning Tasks.</span> Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that our approach consistently improves the accuracy of all PEFT baselines across multiple commonsense reasoning datasets and models. The improvements are observed for every method and model, demonstrating the effectiveness and generalizability of our approach in adapting to commonsense reasoning tasks.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.15888v1/figs/ablation_logit_projection_llama3_1-8b.png" id="S4.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/262;" width="476" height="262" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">LLaMA3.1-8B</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
