            <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 1: Warm-Start Fine-tuning</span> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize task-specific parameter distribution
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
            Split <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}</annotation></semantics></math> into training set <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>train</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> and calibration set <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>calib</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize task-specific parameters <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi\leftarrow\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi\leftarrow\theta</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Start from pre-trained parameters
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            Fine-tune model on <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>train</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Typically 1 epoch is sufficient
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeSteeringVector</span>(<math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              Get base model probabilities: <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}\leftarrow P_{\theta}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}\leftarrow P_{\theta}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              Get fine-tuned model probabilities: <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\phi}\leftarrow P_{\phi}(\cdot|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}\leftarrow P_{\phi}(\cdot|x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 2: Steering Vector Construction</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Capture task-specific direction
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute KL gradient: <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{P}\leftarrow-[\log(p_{\phi}/p_{\theta})+\mathbf{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{P}\leftarrow-[\log(p_{\phi}/p_{\theta})+\mathbf{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Measure distribution mismatch
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute softmax Jacobian: <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\phi})\leftarrow\mathrm{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\phi})\leftarrow\mathrm{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
              Project to logit space: <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}\leftarrow J(p_{\phi})\cdot g_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}\leftarrow J(p_{\phi})\cdot g_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Transform probability gradient to logit space
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 3: Apply Confidence-Aware Constraint</span> <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Filter noise and focus on high-confidence tokens
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
              
              
              Identify most likely token: <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{V}}p_{\phi}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{V}}p_{\phi}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
              
              
              Get threshold probability: <math id="alg1.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mathrm{thresh}}\leftarrow\alpha\cdot p_{\phi}(y^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>thresh</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathrm{thresh}}\leftarrow\alpha\cdot p_{\phi}(y^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
              
              
              Create confidence mask: <math id="alg1.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(y)\leftarrow\mathbf{1}(p_{\phi}(y)\geq p_{\mathrm{thresh}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>thresh</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(y)\leftarrow\mathbf{1}(p_{\phi}(y)\geq p_{\mathrm{thresh}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Binary mask for tokens above threshold
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
              
              
              Apply mask: <math id="alg1.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z}(y)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}(y)\cdot\delta_{z}(y)+(1-\mathbb{I}(y))\cdot\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z}(y)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}(y)\cdot\delta_{z}(y)+(1-\mathbb{I}(y))\cdot\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Apply penalty to low-confidence tokens
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l23.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Return filtered steering vector
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l24.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 4: Calculate Optimal Steering Strength</span> <span id="alg1.l25.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Calibrate <math id="alg1.l25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> using labeled data
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
              
              
            Compute global steering constant <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> from calibration dataset <math id="alg1.l26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>calib</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l26.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> See Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Interpretation. ‣ C.3 Optimal Step Length (Newton Approximation) ‣ Appendix C One-Token Derivation of Optimal Steering Strength 𝜇^∗ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> for details
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage 5: Decoding with Steering Vector</span> <span id="alg1.l27.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Generate task-specific outputs at inference time
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg1.l28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">SteerDecoding</span>(<math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
              Initialize generated sequence: <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\leftarrow[]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\leftarrow[]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each decoding step <math id="alg1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> until completion <span id="alg1.l30.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
               Get current context: <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\leftarrow(x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\leftarrow(x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute task-adapted logits: <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z_{\phi,t}\leftarrow\text{Logits of }P_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext>Logits of </mtext><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi,t}\leftarrow\text{Logits of }P_{\phi}(\cdot|x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z_{t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeSteeringVector}}(x_{t},P_{\theta},P_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeSteeringVector</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z_{t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeSteeringVector}}(x_{t},P_{\theta},P_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">34:</span></span>
              
              
               Adjust logits: <math id="alg1.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{z}_{\phi,t}\leftarrow z_{\phi,t}+\bar{\mu}\cdot\hat{\delta}_{z_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{z}_{\phi,t}\leftarrow z_{\phi,t}+\bar{\mu}\cdot\hat{\delta}_{z_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l34.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Apply steering
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l35.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">35:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute adjusted distribution: <math id="alg1.l35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Softmax}(\hat{z}_{\phi,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Softmax}(\hat{z}_{\phi,t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l36.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">36:</span></span>
              
              
               Sample/select next token <math id="alg1.l36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> according to chosen decoding strategy

</div>
<div id="alg1.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l37.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">37:</span></span>
              
              
               Append to sequence: <math id="alg1.l37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\leftarrow[y,y_{t}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\leftarrow[y,y_{t}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l38.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">38:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l38.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l38.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l39.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l39.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l39.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Complete generated sequence
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l40.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">40:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l40.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l41.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">41:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l41.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <span id="alg1.l41.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">SteerDecoding</span> function <span id="alg1.l41.5" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Return configured decoding function for inference
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this appendix, we prove that a <em id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">first-order</em> Steering-Vector-Decoding (SVD) step is equivalent, in expectation, to one parameter-update step of maximum-likelihood fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Notation and Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\theta}(x)\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the logits produced by the pre-trained LLM for input <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\theta}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\theta}(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.
After a short warm-start fine-tuning, the parameters are <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, giving logits <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> and distribution
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a downstream dataset
<math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,
the standard fine-tuning objective is the expected negative log-likelihood (NLL):</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FT}}(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}}[\log p_{\theta}(y\mid x)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>task</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FT}}(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{task}}}[\log p_{\theta}(y\mid x)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is equivalent to <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>
up to an additive constant, where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>task</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the empirical one-hot distribution.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KL-Gradient Steering Signal.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Section <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Steering Vector Construction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> derives the task-aware direction in probability space as</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{P}=-\nabla_{p_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(p_{\phi}\|p_{\theta})=-\bigl[\log(\frac{p_{\phi}}{p_{\theta}})+\mathbf{1}\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{P}=-\nabla_{p_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(p_{\phi}\|p_{\theta})=-\bigl[\log(\frac{p_{\phi}}{p_{\theta}})+\mathbf{1}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which is then projected into logit space via the softmax Jacobian:</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\phi})=\operatorname{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\!\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\phi})=\operatorname{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\!\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the logit-space steering vector is:</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}~=~J(p_{\phi})\,g_{P}~=~\bigl(\operatorname{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\!\top}\bigr)\,\bigl[-\log(\frac{p_{\phi}}{p_{\theta}})-\mathbf{1}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}~=~J(p_{\phi})\,g_{P}~=~\bigl(\operatorname{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\!\top}\bigr)\,\bigl[-\log(\frac{p_{\phi}}{p_{\theta}})-\mathbf{1}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Fine-Tuning Gradient in Logit Space</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a single training pair <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{\ast})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{\ast})</annotation></semantics></math> the NLL loss is</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log p(y^{\ast}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log p(y^{\ast}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\log\left(\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{y^{\ast}})\right)=-\log\frac{e^{z_{y^{\ast}}}}{\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\log\left(\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{y^{\ast}})\right)=-\log\frac{e^{z_{y^{\ast}}}}{\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E25Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-z_{y^{\ast}}+\log\!\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-z_{y^{\ast}}+\log\!\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Its gradient w.r.t. logits is</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z}\ell=p-e_{y^{\ast}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>z</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z}\ell=p-e_{y^{\ast}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one-hot vector for the correct token.
Taking the dataset expectation:</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FT}}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{\ast})}[\,p_{\phi}-\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>FT</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>task</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FT}}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{\ast})}[\,p_{\phi}-\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>task</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\mathrm{task}}</annotation></semantics></math> is one-hot, this is the steepest-descent direction that moves <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> toward the true task distribution.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Derivation of the Gradient</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To derive <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{z}\ell=p-e_{y^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>z</mi></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z}\ell=p-e_{y^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the partial derivative of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(z)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to each logit <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partial derivative of <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-z_{y^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-z_{y^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>: If <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(-z_{y^{*}})}{\partial z_{k}}=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(-z_{y^{*}})}{\partial z_{k}}=-1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\neq y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\neq y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial(-z_{y^{*}})}{\partial z_{k}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial(-z_{y^{*}})}{\partial z_{k}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
This can be written as <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of the one-hot vector <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partial derivative of <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>: The derivative is <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{e^{z_{k}}}{\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}}=p_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{e^{z_{k}}}{\sum_{y}e^{z_{y}}}=p_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{Softmax}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{Softmax}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Combining these, the partial derivative is:</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\ell(z)}{\partial z_{k}}=p_{k}-[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\ell(z)}{\partial z_{k}}=p_{k}-[e_{y^{*}}]_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus, the gradient vector is given by Eq. <a href="#A2.E26" title="In B.2 Fine-Tuning Gradient in Logit Space ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>One SVD Step in Logit Space</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SVD perturbs logits during decoding by</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}~=~z_{\phi}\;+\;\mu\cdot\delta_{z},\qquad\;\tilde{p}~=~\mathrm{Softmax}(\tilde{z})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.608em" rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.447em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}~=~z_{\phi}\;+\;\mu\cdot\delta_{z},\qquad\;\tilde{p}~=~\mathrm{Softmax}(\tilde{z}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> is given in Eq. <a href="#A2.E24" title="In KL-Gradient Steering Signal. ‣ B.1 Notation and Preliminaries ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar strength (estimated in Appendix C).
Because the perturbation is before the softmax, <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is always a valid probability distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>First-Order Equivalence Theorem</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> be fixed and let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\phi}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> be the warm-started distribution. For any label distribution <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and any strength <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the KL divergence after one SVD step by</span></p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{K}(\mu)=\mathrm{KL}(q\|\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi}+\mu\delta_{z}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(\mu)=\mathrm{KL}(q\|\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi}+\mu\delta_{z})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Bigl.\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}\Bigr|_{\mu=0}=\bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi}),\delta z\bigr\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl.\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}\Bigr|_{\mu=0}=\bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi}),\delta z\bigr\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\hat{p}_{\text{task}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">task</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\hat{p}_{\text{task}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by <em id="Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">any</em> fine-tuning algorithm that has converged to a stationary point
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\!\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi})=\mathbf{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\!\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi})=\mathbf{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, then
<math id="Thmtheorem2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)/\partial\mu|_{\mu=0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)/\partial\mu|_{\mu=0}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence an infinitesimal SVD step leaves the fine-tuning objective unchanged up to <math id="Thmtheorem2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\mu^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\mu^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\frac{\partial\tilde{z}}{\partial\mu}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\frac{1}{\partial\mu}\cdot(z_{\phi}+\mu\delta_{z})=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\frac{\partial\tilde{z}}{\partial\mu}=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\frac{1}{\partial\mu}\cdot(z_{\phi}+\mu\delta_{z})=\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}}{\partial\tilde{z}}\cdot\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E32Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{\tilde{z}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|\tilde{p}),\delta_{z}\bigr\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{\tilde{z}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|\tilde{p}),\delta_{z}\bigr\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}=\mathrm{Softmax}(\tilde{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}=\mathrm{Softmax}(\tilde{z})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{z}=z_{\phi}+\mu\cdot\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{z}=z_{\phi}+\mu\cdot\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}=p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}=p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, so we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Bigl.\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}\Bigr|_{\mu=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Bigl.\frac{\partial\mathcal{K}(\mu)}{\partial\mu}\Bigr|_{\mu=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{\tilde{z}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|\tilde{p})\Bigr|_{\mu=0},\delta z\bigr\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>z</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{\tilde{z}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|\tilde{p})\Bigr|_{\mu=0},\delta z\bigr\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E33Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi}),\delta z\bigr\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(q\|p_{\phi}),\delta z\bigr\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which gives the same result as Eq. <a href="#A2.E31" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ B.4 First-Order Equivalence Theorem ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>.
If <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> is at a stationary point of <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(q\|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(q\|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>,
the inner product vanishes. A full Taylor expansion shows
<math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(\mu)=\mathcal{K}(0)+O(\mu^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(\mu)=\mathcal{K}(0)+O(\mu^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. <a href="#A2.E31" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ B.4 First-Order Equivalence Theorem ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a> states that the first-order of the KL objective reacts to an SVD step exactly as it reacts to a gradient step of fine-tuning. Therefore SVD and fine-tuning are locally equivalent in the space of output distributions, even though one edits logits at decode time while the other edits weights during training.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Conditions for Higher-Order Equivalence</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ B.4 First-Order Equivalence Theorem ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> guarantees local equivalence. Exact global equivalence holds when
(i) the steering direction lies in the span of the fine-tuning gradient subspace across all inputs,
and (ii) <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> follows the continuous-time ordinary differential equation <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dot{\mu}(t)=\eta\,\mu^{\star}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dot{\mu}(t)=\eta\,\mu^{\star}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for learning-rate <math id="A2.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice we use a single discrete step per token, which is sufficient to capture the empirical gains reported in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, SVD can be viewed as an <em id="A2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">on-the-fly proxy</em> for one gradient step of fine-tuning, executed in logit space with provable first-order equivalence but <em id="A2.SS5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">without</em> the memory or time overhead of back-propagation. This theoretical link explains why combining SVD with any PEFT method consistently improves performance while preserving efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>One-Token Derivation of Optimal Steering Strength <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Setup.</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}</annotation></semantics></math> be the warm-started logits for an input <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>
and let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> the task-aware steering vector obtained from the Jacobian-projected KL gradient in Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.1 Steering Vector Construction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.
At decode time we can form perturbed logits:</p>
<table id="A3.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\mu}=z_{\phi}+\mu\cdot\delta_{z},\quad p_{\mu}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\mu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\mu}=z_{\phi}+\mu\cdot\delta_{z},\quad p_{\mu}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to choose a scalar strength <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> that <em id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">locally</em> reduces the true objective
<math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math>
as much as possible, while keeping the computation lightweight.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>First-Order Taylor Expansion of KL</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because a single decoding step is small, expand the KL divergence around
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})~=~\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})\;+\;\mu\,\underbrace{\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\;\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle}_{\text{linear term}}\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mu^{2}\,\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]+\mathcal{O}(\mu^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.608em">=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>μ</mi><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>linear term</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})~=~\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})\;+\;\mu\,\underbrace{\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\;\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle}_{\text{linear term}}\;+\;\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mu^{2}\,\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]+\mathcal{O}(\mu^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where
<math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]=\delta_{z}^{\top}\,\nabla^{2}_{z_{\phi}}\,\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})\,\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]=\delta_{z}^{\top}\,\nabla^{2}_{z_{\phi}}\,\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})\,\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the quadratic form of the Hessian.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Optimal Step Length (Newton Approximation)</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To find the optimal
step length <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, that minimizes <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\mu})</annotation></semantics></math>, we ignore the constant zeroth-order term and the higher-order terms <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\mu^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\mu^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider only the first two orders:</p>
<table id="A3.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\mu)=\mu\cdot\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mu)=\mu\cdot\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\mu^{2}\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then, we take the derivative of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and set it to zero:</p>
<table id="A3.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\mu}f(\mu)=\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle+\mu\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\mu}f(\mu)=\Bigl\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\Bigr\rangle+\mu\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Solving for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</p>
<table id="A3.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}=-\frac{\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\rangle}{\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}=-\frac{\langle\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi}),\delta_{z}\rangle}{\mathcal{H}[\delta_{z}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which is the exact Newton step.
For a one-hot ground-truth label <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> the task distribution
is <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{\mathrm{task}}(y)=\mathbf{1}_{\{y=y^{*}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\mathrm{task}}(y)=\mathbf{1}_{\{y=y^{*}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the gradient of the KL divergence is formulated as follows which can be recalled from Eq. <a href="#A2.E26" title="In B.2 Fine-Tuning Gradient in Logit Space ‣ Appendix B Mathematical Analysis: Equivalence Between SVD and Fine-Tuning ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>:</p>
<table id="A3.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})=p_{\phi}-e_{y^{*}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{z_{\phi}}\mathrm{KL}(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|p_{\phi})=p_{\phi}-e_{y^{*}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one-hot basis vector for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting this into the expression for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</p>
<table id="A3.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}=-\frac{\langle p_{\phi}-e_{y^{*}},\,\delta z\rangle}{\mathcal{H}[\delta z]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}=-\frac{\langle p_{\phi}-e_{y^{*}},\,\delta z\rangle}{\mathcal{H}[\delta z]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This derivation shows that the optimal
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the negative ratio of the linear term to the quadratic term in the Taylor expansion. The exact Newton step requires computing the Hessian <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}[\delta z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}[\delta z]</annotation></semantics></math>. However, computing the full Hessian is expensive. We therefore adopt the common <em id="A3.SS3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Gauss–Newton</em> approximation
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}[\delta z]\approx\lVert\delta z\rVert^{2}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≈</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}[\delta z]\approx\lVert\delta z\rVert^{2}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
(which is exact for a quadratic loss), yielding</p>
<table id="A3.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu^{*}=\frac{\bigl\langle e_{y^{*}}-p_{\phi},\;\delta_{z}\bigr\rangle}{\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert^{2}_{2}\;+\;\epsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>μ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}=\frac{\bigl\langle e_{y^{*}}-p_{\phi},\;\delta_{z}\bigr\rangle}{\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert^{2}_{2}\;+\;\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where a small <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-12}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-12}</annotation></semantics></math>) prevents division by zero when
<math id="A3.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is tiny.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interpretation.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Eq. <a href="#A3.E41" title="In C.3 Optimal Step Length (Newton Approximation) ‣ Appendix C One-Token Derivation of Optimal Steering Strength 𝜇^∗ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> projects the desired probability-mass shift
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(e_{y^{*}}-p_{\phi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(e_{y^{*}}-p_{\phi})</annotation></semantics></math> onto the steering direction <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>; the scalar
ratio tells us how far to move along <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> so that the first-order
drop in KL is maximal.
If <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert_{2}&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{z}\rVert_{2}&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> we fall back to a small default
<math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>) or simply skip steering for that
token.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Computing the Global Steering Constant <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              Pre-trained LLM <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              Warm-started (fine-tuned) LLM <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}(y|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}(y|x)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
              Task-specific labeled dataset <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>calib</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> for calibration

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              Confidence threshold <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
              Small constant <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> to prevent division by zero

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
              Task-specific global steering constant <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeTokenSteeringVector</span>(<math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
                Compute KL-gradient: <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{P}\leftarrow-[\log(p_{\phi}/p_{\theta})+\mathbf{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{P}\leftarrow-[\log(p_{\phi}/p_{\theta})+\mathbf{1}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
                Compute softmax Jacobian: <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(p_{\phi})\leftarrow\mathrm{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(p_{\phi})\leftarrow\mathrm{diag}(p_{\phi})-p_{\phi}p_{\phi}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
                
                
                Project to logit space: <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}\leftarrow J(p_{\phi})\cdot g_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}\leftarrow J(p_{\phi})\cdot g_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg2.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeConfidenceAwareConstraint</span>(<math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
                
                
                Identify most likely token: <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{V}}p_{\phi}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{y\in\mathcal{V}}p_{\phi}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
                
                
                Create confidence mask: <math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(y)\leftarrow\mathbf{1}(p_{\phi}(y)\geq\alpha\cdot p_{\phi}(y^{*}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(y)\leftarrow\mathbf{1}(p_{\phi}(y)\geq\alpha\cdot p_{\phi}(y^{*}))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
                
                
                Apply mask: <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z}(y)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}(y)\cdot\delta_{z}(y)+(1-\mathbb{I}(y))\cdot\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z}(y)\leftarrow\mathbb{I}(y)\cdot\delta_{z}(y)+(1-\mathbb{I}(y))\cdot\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span> <span id="alg2.l20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeTokenwiseMu</span>(<math id="alg2.l20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
                
                
                Initialize empty set <math id="alg2.l21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> to collect token-level <math id="alg2.l21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> values

</div>
<div id="alg2.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each token position <math id="alg2.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in sequence <math id="alg2.l22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
                
                
                 Get model logits: <math id="alg2.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\phi,i,t}\leftarrow\text{Logits of }P_{\phi}\text{ for }(x_{i},y_{i,&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>Logits of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi,i,t}\leftarrow\text{Logits of }P_{\phi}\text{ for }(x_{i},y_{i,&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
                
                
                 Compute probabilities: <math id="alg2.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi,i,t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi,i,t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
                
                
                 Get probabilities from base model: <math id="alg2.l25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta,i,t}\leftarrow P_{\theta}(y|x_{i},y_{i,&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta,i,t}\leftarrow P_{\theta}(y|x_{i},y_{i,&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
                
                
                 Get ground truth token: <math id="alg2.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,t}^{*}\leftarrow y_{i}[t]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,t}^{*}\leftarrow y_{i}[t]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
                
                
                 Create one-hot distribution: <math id="alg2.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}\leftarrow\mathrm{OneHot}(y_{i,t}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>OneHot</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}\leftarrow\mathrm{OneHot}(y_{i,t}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{z_{i,t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeTokenSteeringVector}}(p_{\phi,i,t},p_{\theta,i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeTokenSteeringVector</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{z_{i,t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeTokenSteeringVector}}(p_{\phi,i,t},p_{\theta,i,t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeConfidenceAwareConstraint}}(\delta_{z_{i,t}},p_{\phi,i,t},\alpha,-\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeConfidenceAwareConstraint</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeConfidenceAwareConstraint}}(\delta_{z_{i,t}},p_{\phi,i,t},\alpha,-\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
                
                
                 Compute optimal token-level strength:

</div>
<div id="alg2.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
                
                
                 <math id="alg2.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}\leftarrow\frac{\langle e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,i,t},\,\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\rangle}{\|\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\|_{2}^{2}+\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}\leftarrow\frac{\langle e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,i,t},\,\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\rangle}{\|\hat{\delta}_{z_{i,t}}\|_{2}^{2}+\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
                
                
                 Add to collection: <math id="alg2.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\{(i,t,\mu_{i,t}^{*})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\{(i,t,\mu_{i,t}^{*})\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l33.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l33.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">34:</span></span>
                
                
                <span id="alg2.l34.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l35.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">35:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l35.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l35.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">function</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l36.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">36:</span></span>
                
                
              Initialize empty collection <math id="alg2.l36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l37.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">37:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l37.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each sample <math id="alg2.l37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg2.l37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>calib</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathrm{calib}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l37.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l38.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">38:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{i}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeTokenwiseMu}}(x_{i},y_{i},P_{\phi},P_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">ComputeTokenwiseMu</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{i}\leftarrow\texttt{{ComputeTokenwiseMu}}(x_{i},y_{i},P_{\phi},P_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l39.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg2.l39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\mathcal{S}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\mathcal{S}\cup\mathcal{S}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l40.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">40:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l40.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l40.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l41" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l41.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">41:</span></span>
                
                
              Compute mean steering strength: <math id="alg2.l41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{(i,t,\mu_{i,t}^{*})\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}\leftarrow\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{(i,t,\mu_{i,t}^{*})\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l42" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l42.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">42:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg2.l42.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>One-Token and Dataset-Level Derivation of the Offline Steering Strength <math id="A4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive here a two-stage procedure: 1) compute the per-token optimal strength <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> on a <em id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">labelled</em> calibration split (training or validation set), and 2) aggregate these values into a single, task-specific constant <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> that is reused for <em id="A4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">all</em> decoding steps at test time. The detailed algorithm is shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ Interpretation. ‣ C.3 Optimal Step Length (Newton Approximation) ‣ Appendix C One-Token Derivation of Optimal Steering Strength 𝜇^∗ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Per-token optimal strength <math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For sentence <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and position <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> let
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\phi,i,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi,i,t}\in\mathbb{R}^{|V|}</annotation></semantics></math>
be the warm-started logits,
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi,i,t}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi,i,t}=\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,t}^{*}\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,t}^{*}\in V</annotation></semantics></math> the ground-truth token.
The Jacobian-projected KL-gradient steering vector
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta z_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta z_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math>
is given by Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.1 Steering Vector Construction ‣ 3 Method ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Local KL Objective.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We seek a scalar <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> that decreases</p>
<table id="A4.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\bigl(e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}\|\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t}+\mu\,\delta_{z_{i,t}})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\bigl(e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}\|\mathrm{Softmax}(z_{\phi,i,t}+\mu\,\delta_{z_{i,t}})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the one-hot target distribution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Gauss-Newton Step.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A first-order Taylor expansion around <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0</annotation></semantics></math>
combined with the Gauss-Newton Hessian approximation
<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\delta_{z_{i,t}}\rVert_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\delta_{z_{i,t}}\rVert_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
yields the optimal step length:</p>
<table id="A4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}=\frac{\bigl\langle e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,i,t},\;\delta_{z_{i,t}}\bigr\rangle}{\lVert\delta_{z_{i,t}}\rVert_{2}^{2}+\epsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}=\frac{\bigl\langle e_{y_{i,t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,i,t},\;\delta_{z_{i,t}}\bigr\rangle}{\lVert\delta_{z_{i,t}}\rVert_{2}^{2}+\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is a small constant to prevent division by zero. This is identical in form to Eq. <a href="#A3.E41" title="In C.3 Optimal Step Length (Newton Approximation) ‣ Appendix C One-Token Derivation of Optimal Steering Strength 𝜇^∗ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>From Tokens to a Global Constant <math id="A4.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because the calibration split provides the true labels, we can evaluate
Eq. <a href="#A4.E43" title="In Gauss-Newton Step. ‣ D.1 Per-token optimal strength 𝜇_{𝑖,𝑡}^∗ ‣ Appendix D One-Token and Dataset-Level Derivation of the Offline Steering Strength 𝜇̄ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a> for every token whose prediction is made
by the warm-started model. Let <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> denote this collection of
indices <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,t)</annotation></semantics></math>. The simplest unbiased estimator is the arithmetic mean:</p>
<table id="A4.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{(i,t)\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{i,t}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}|}\sum_{(i,t)\in\mathcal{S}}\mu_{i,t}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">However, if the distribution of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i,t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i,t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is heavy-tailed, we can replace the mean by the median or a trimmed mean:</p>
<table id="A4.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}=\operatorname{median}\bigl\{\mu_{i,t}^{*}\bigr\}\quad\text{or}\quad\bar{\mu}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}_{\tau}|}\sum_{(i,t)\in\mathcal{S}_{\tau}}\mu_{i,t}^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>median</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}=\operatorname{median}\bigl\{\mu_{i,t}^{*}\bigr\}\quad\text{or}\quad\bar{\mu}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{S}_{\tau}|}\sum_{(i,t)\in\mathcal{S}_{\tau}}\mu_{i,t}^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{\tau}=\{(i,t):|\mu_{i,t}^{*}-m|&lt;\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{\tau}=\{(i,t):|\mu_{i,t}^{*}-m|&lt;\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a central <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-trimmed subset around the median <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. In all our experiments we adopt the plain mean formulated in Eq. <a href="#A4.E44" title="In D.2 From Tokens to a Global Constant 𝜇̄ ‣ Appendix D One-Token and Dataset-Level Derivation of the Offline Steering Strength 𝜇̄ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>, which already works well.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This scalar <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> not only captures the dominant shift dictated by the task distribution but also preserves the key advantage of SVD: <em id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">no run-time optimisation loop and no per-token label needed</em>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Extension to sequences (<math id="A4.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The derivation in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Per-token optimal strength 𝜇_{𝑖,𝑡}^∗ ‣ Appendix D One-Token and Dataset-Level Derivation of the Offline Steering Strength 𝜇̄ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> treats one decoding step in isolation.
For an <em id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">autoregressive</em> sequence <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=(y_{1},\dots,y_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(y_{1},\dots,y_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> the joint
likelihood factorises
<math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\phi}(y\mid x)=\prod_{t=1}^{T}p_{\phi,t}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\phi}(y\mid x)=\prod_{t=1}^{T}p_{\phi,t}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the sequence-level KL objective is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\bigl(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|P_{\phi}\bigr)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathrm{KL}\bigl(e_{y_{t}^{*}}\|p_{\phi,t}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>task</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\bigl(P_{\mathrm{task}}\|P_{\phi}\bigr)=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathrm{KL}\bigl(e_{y_{t}^{*}}\|p_{\phi,t}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because each term depends only on its local logits <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\phi,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\phi,t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
first-order "Newton in <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>” argument extends verbatim:
the optimal <em id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">global</em> strength that minimises the quadratic
approximation of the total KL is</p>
<table id="A4.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu^{*}_{1:T}=\frac{\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl\langle e_{y_{t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,t},\,\delta z_{t}\bigr\rangle}{\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lVert\delta z_{t}\rVert_{2}^{2}+T\epsilon}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu^{*}_{1:T}=\frac{\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\bigl\langle e_{y_{t}^{*}}-p_{\phi,t},\,\delta z_{t}\bigr\rangle}{\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{T}\lVert\delta z_{t}\rVert_{2}^{2}+T\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is the token-wise numerator and denominator from Eq. <a href="#A4.E43" title="In Gauss-Newton Step. ‣ D.1 Per-token optimal strength 𝜇_{𝑖,𝑡}^∗ ‣ Appendix D One-Token and Dataset-Level Derivation of the Offline Steering Strength 𝜇̄ ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a> summed over <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Gauss–Newton Hessian remains block-diagonal, so cross-time Jacobian
terms cancel in the same first-order limit.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Experiment Implementation Details</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Implementation Details of SVD</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the implementation details of the SVD method. It is summarized in the following Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ E.1 Implementation Details of SVD ‣ Appendix E Experiment Implementation Details ‣ Distribution-Aligned Decoding for Efficient LLM Task Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 6</span>: </span><span id="A5.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Implementation Details of SVD.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T6.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T6.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt">Parameter</td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt">Value/Setting</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Warm-start Steps (Epochs)</td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r"><math id="A5.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> in Confidence-aware Constraint</td>
<td id="A5.T6.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.1</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T6.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T6.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r"><math id="A5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in Confidence-aware Constraint</td>
